  "reason": "The current best (config_002, acc=0.6352) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder with imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, and weighted fusion. The only major untested dimension in this otherwise-validated configuration is the RNA encoder. config_036 swaps pca_n2000 for scvi_n200 while keeping all other settings identical (multimodal, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted), providing a clean A/B test of whether a learned nonlinear RNA representation outperforms linear PCA. This is the highest-value next experiment because: (1) it directly exploits the strongest configuration found so far, (2) it tests the single most impactful unexplored variable (RNA encoder quality), and (3) with 5 experiments remaining, a positive result would open a clear exploitation path (e.g., then testing scgpt), while a negative result would confirm PCA's sufficiency and redirect budget toward image encoder or profile-setting variations."
}

